     While Apache Kafka is[0m[2m famous for handling millions of messages per second, our 10x scaling target requires handling peak volumes of 5,[0m[2m000 requests per second. Redis Streams, running entirely in-memory, easily achieves throughputs exceeding 10[0m[2m0,000 write/read operations per second per node under standard workloads. A single Redis node or highly available[0m[2m Redis Sentinel/Cluster setup can handle our 10x peak traffic with sub-millisecond latencies, making its[0m[2m performance more than sufficient for our requirements.
     
